// title: "Highway domain registry"
// summary: "Reserve the highway domain’s registry and implementation locations while no highway pieces are implemented."
//
// Used when: The library loads its registered transport domains for commands such as list, inventory, or scaffold; this reserved domain currently contains no pieces, assemblies, or implementation module.
//
// Read by: custom-pieces/framework/scp/catalog.py load_catalog() reads this registry through project.jsonc, loads its collections file, and follows only explicitly listed subject paths; scp.providers.implementation() reads the implementation field and rejects its current null value if highway implementation is requested.
//
// Updated by: Contributors deliberately register highway subjects and implementation routing here; custom-pieces/scp.py scaffold --domain highway and scp.registration.apply_registration() can add draft piece entries with the header-preserving JSONC writer.
//
// Affects: The highway catalogue membership, collection location, future implementation routing, and scaffold dependency and menu defaults; the empty registry creates no highway model, build output, or in-game button.
//
// Reference: custom-pieces/domains/highway/AGENTS.md
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "purpose": "Explicit registry of maintained pieces, documented assemblies, implementation and build collections for this transport domain.",
  "id": "highway",
  "name": "Highway (reserved; no pieces implemented)",
  "implementation": null,
  "pieces": [],
  "assemblies": [],
  "collections": "collections.jsonc",
  "scaffold": {
    "dependencies": [
      "controller"
    ],
    "menu_style": "draft"
  }
}
